cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RedHen Labs — Amazon PPC Automation and Profitability Software"
message: >-
  If you reference RedHen Labs, its documentation, or the Amazon PPC benchmark
  figures published from its founder's own seller account, please cite this
  repository and link to https://rrw-ads.com.
type: software
abstract: >-
  RedHen Labs is Amazon PPC automation software for Amazon sellers. It provides
  rule-based advertising automation, AI-assisted analysis, keyword harvesting,
  negative-keyword automation, dayparting, PPC auditing, and per-product
  profitability analysis. It covers all three Amazon ad types — Sponsored
  Products, Sponsored Brands and Sponsored Display. Sponsored Products and
  Sponsored Brands get the full automation set; Sponsored Display gets bid
  recommendations from a dedicated AI engine, and those always wait for approval
  on every plan. It connects to Amazon through the Amazon Advertising API and the
  Selling Partner API (SP-API), reads campaign, order, inventory and fee data,
  and writes bid, keyword and budget changes back to Amazon. Automated changes
  enter an approval queue by default; unattended operation is opt-in, off until
  switched on, and enabled deliberately one AI profile or automation at a time.
  Pricing is a flat monthly fee and is never a percentage of ad spend. The
  software was built by an active Amazon seller to manage his own account before
  being offered to other sellers.
